SUMMARY:Bobby McFerrin's MOTION
DESCRIPTION:In 2021\, Bobby McFerrin asked David Worm to bring together singers to play and improvise together. The result is MOTION\, a collective of masterful vocalists and facilitators dedicated to the transformational potential of improvised sound. Bryan Dyer\, David Worm\, and Destani Wolf have joined Bobby on stage and in the studio\, creating songs in the moment\, facilitating Circlesinging\, harmonizing and connecting their intuitive voices weekly for 4 years as the band MOTION. They continue to perform and create vocal community space to honor healing and peace\, every Monday at The Freight in Berkeley. \nThe Bay Area has been washed in the powerful and heart felt vocals of each member of acapella band MOTION since they started their musical journeys in their hometowns of Berkeley\, Oakland\, and Los Altos Hills. Bryan Dyer\, David Worm\, and Destani Wolf’s individual paths have taken them around the globe\, recording and performing with the best. From Quincy Jones\, Michael McDonald\, Ladysmith Black Mambazo\, The Pharcyde\, John Cale\, on Grammy nominated albums to vocal collaborations with multidisciplinary arts such as Cirque du Soleil\, Robert Moses Kin\, Bandaloop\, Tandy Beal and Axis Dance. Besides their voices and compositions being including in TV and film (Disney’s “The Descendants”\, HBO’s “Momentum Generation”\, “Set up” Benjamin Bratt’s “The Mission”\, Kevin Harts: “Laugh at my Pain”\, FOX’s “SYTYCD” and more) they are veteran acapella vocalists dedicated to using their voices to empower and inspire hope and create positive change in their communities and worldwide. \nMOTION shares a collective vision of music and the voice healing ourselves and the world. They have taught vocal technique\, improv\, circle singing at world renowned learning institutes like Omega Institute in New York\, The Esalen Institute in Big Sur California\, The Berkeley School of Music\, San Francisco Music Conservatory\, UCLA\, Living Jazz\, to name a few. Together they are enlightened and inspired by performing and facilitated classes and workshops in the hopes of illuminating open heart’s and building community through song. \nFriday\, June 5th\, at 8:30pm. Admission is free!
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/bobby-mcferrins-motion/
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater\, 115 North Street\, Healdsburg\, 95448
CATEGORIES:Music
END:VEVENT
